Build for a free Personal Team: Local signing only, signed for seven days, no paid membership needed.

A free Apple Account's Personal Team cannot sign the Network Extension (Developer service's tunnel) or
extended virtual addressing, so the Tolkara target, which carries both and embeds the tunnel, cannot be
built with one. TOLKARA_SIGNING=personal builds TolkaraPersonal instead: the same app (AppBase, built as
Tolkara.app with the same identifier and Home Screen name) without the tunnel or TOLKARA_INTEGRATED_AUTH,
signed with launcher/Personal.entitlements (the increased memory limit, which Apple's capability table does
not list) or, when the team is refused that, launcher/Personal-Plain.entitlements (none); both are layer
files (pocket/launcher/Personal/, overlay.map). It requires TOLKARA_MODE=local-signing. The client reserves
little address space (3.1 MB at most with mmap, docs/client-analysis.md), so extended virtual addressing is
not expected to matter; whether its heap (about 1 GB) fits a phone's limit without the increased memory
limit is to be measured on a device.

Brighter Pocket Companion accepts a free team: it is chosen by itself when it is the only team, the Developer
Account step says the signature lasts seven days, the Install step shows Local signing without the choice of
Developer service and warns two days before the signature ends, and local.env carries TOLKARA_SIGNING. A
team not known to be free that Xcode refuses as a Personal Team is marked free and built again that way.
Upstream candidate: Tolkara's own README offers free signing only through External JIT; a Personal Team
build of the app for Local signing would serve any game that fits in memory.

